# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — RustyNES
#
# ORDER MATTERS: a `!` negation re-includes only what the rules ABOVE it
# ignored, and a later rule ignores again. Keep a new rule on the correct side
# of the negations it interacts with (the golden, coverage and nestest
# re-includes below).
#
# A bare pattern (no `/` except a trailing one) matches at ANY depth. Before
# adding one, check it against the tree: `git ls-files -ci --exclude-standard`
# lists the tracked files an ignore rule would hide.
# =============================================================================

# --- Rust / Cargo ---
/target/
# Nested per-crate target/ dirs (the root /target/ rule is anchored).
crates/*/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.bench
# Track the lockfiles of the binary workspace and of `crates/rustynes-cosim`,
# which is excluded from the workspace and resolves its own graph. The cosim
# crate emits the goldens an external NES implementation is verified against,
# so its resolve is provenance and must not move unrecorded (v2.4.2). The bare
# `Cargo.lock` matches at any depth: name every lockfile that is kept.
Cargo.lock
!/Cargo.lock
!/crates/rustynes-cosim/Cargo.lock

# --- Golden-export output ---
# `nes_golden_export` and the sibling's gates write these wherever `--out`
# points. They are reproducible from a pinned commit, so none belong in the
# tree. When a co-simulation rung adds a format, add its suffix here (the list
# fell behind four times); check with
#   for s in ckpt obs boot index_fb ram ram_init fetch apu dut; do
#     git check-ignore -q "x.$s.bin" || echo "NOT IGNORED: $s"; done
# `*.ram.bin` does not match `<stem>.ram_init.bin`; both are needed.
*.ckpt.bin
*.obs.bin
*.boot.bin
*.index_fb.bin
*.ram.bin
*.ram_init.bin
*.fetch.bin
*.irq.csv
*.dut.bin
*.apu.bin
# Deliberately broad: the exporter names it `<rom-stem>.manifest.txt`. If a
# manifest ever needs tracking, re-include it explicitly.
*.manifest.txt
# The committed golden trees, named so a golden added there is not swallowed.
!/golden/**
!/crates/rustynes-test-harness/golden/**

# --- Native build & FFI artifacts ---
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe
*.a
*.lib
*.pdb
# Apple debug symbols: the libretro Apple jobs and the iOS xcframework build
# leave `<name>.dylib.dSYM` bundles (and the buildbot's zip of them) beside the
# library.
*.dSYM/
*.dSYM.zip

# --- WebAssembly / trunk / wasm-pack ---
/pkg/
/dist/
*.wasm
wasm-pack.log
/crates/rustynes-frontend/web/dist/
# The Emscripten rcheevos side module's JS glue
# (`scripts/cheevos/build_rcheevos_wasm.sh`); the hand-written `ra_glue.js` and
# the directory's README are tracked.
/crates/rustynes-frontend/web/cheevos/rcheevos.js

# --- Node.js ---
node_modules/
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
# The hosted services are deployed from CI-tested code, so `npm ci` must
# reproduce the tree the tests ran against: their lockfile is tracked.
!/services/hosted/package-lock.json
# wrangler's local dev state and `wrangler dev` secrets.
/services/hosted/.wrangler/
/services/hosted/.dev.vars

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
# Icon generator default output (make_icon.py).
/assets/RustyNES_Icon/out/

# --- Platform packages ---
*.AppImage
*.snap
*.flatpak
*.msi
*.appx
# insta's committed reference snapshots also end in `.snap`: re-include them
# (`/**/` also matches zero directories). Pending or rejected ones
# (`.snap.new`) are accepted or deleted, never committed.
!**/snapshots/**/*.snap
*.snap.new

# --- Fuzzing (commit the harnesses; ignore the build and corpus) ---
fuzz/
!/fuzz/
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/
corpus/
artifacts/

# --- ROMs, disks, music, patches (copyright) ---
# All ROMs are ignored; the committable test-ROM suites under tests/roms/ are
# re-included (licences per file in REUSE.toml and tests/roms/LICENSES.md).
# Commercial dumps, BestEffort boot-smoke ROMs included, live under
# tests/roms/external/ and are NEVER committed.
*.nes
*.fds
!/tests/roms/**/*.nes
# No trailing slash: a git worktree reaches the main tree's dumps through a
# SYMLINK at this path, which a `dir/` pattern does not match (v2.9.8).
/tests/roms/external
/tests/roms/nes-test-roms/
/game-roms/
*.qd
*.nsf
*.nsfe
*.nsf2
# User-supplied palettes; none are committed.
*.pal
# ROM soft-patches (auto-applied beside a ROM) and the live-patch recorder's
# RAM-pin sidecar: user material, handled like the ROMs.
*.ips
*.ups
*.bps
*.pins.toml

# --- TAS movies (may contain copyrighted content) ---
*.rnm
*.rnmproj
*.rnmb
*.fm2
*.fm3
*.bk2
*.tasproj

# --- Saves, states, input recordings, dumps, cheats ---
*.rns
*.sav
*.srm
*.state
*.savestate
*.snapshot
*.rec
*.input
*.ram
*.dump
*.cht

# --- Game databases ---
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.dat
*.xml
!assets/**/*.xml
# The ROM-Database editor's user overlay, if the app is run from the repo root.
game_db_user.txt
# The NES 2.0 DB the Game Genie re-key reads at build time.
scripts/gg/nes20db.xml

# --- Logs / debug / test output ---
*.log
# The kevtris nestest golden trace is tracked despite `*.log`.
!/tests/roms/nestest/nestest.log
*.golden
test-output/
/tests/captures/
/tests/framework/enhanced-validator/target/
/tests/framework/test_rom_validator

# --- Coverage / profiling ---
*.gcno
*.gcda
coverage/
# `coverage/` is for coverage-artifact dirs, not the committed tooling; the
# tooling's library-header cache and bytecode stay ignored.
!/scripts/coverage/
!/scripts/coverage/**
/scripts/coverage/.library-index.json
/scripts/coverage/__pycache__/
tarpaulin-report.html
perf.data
perf.data.old
flamegraph.svg
/perf-logs/
# PGO profiles (pgo.yml, scripts/pgo/), regenerated by the recipe.
*.profraw
*.profdata
/pgo-data/

# --- Documentation build output and local-only references ---
/docs/_site/
# MkDocs Material's social-card and privacy plugin cache (`mkdocs build`).
/.cache/
# Engine-development audit history, kept locally, not in the public repo.
/docs/audit/
# The local NESdev wiki mirror (~208 MB, reference only).
/nesdev_wiki/
# Third-party Alliance Memory SDRAM datasheets, marked "Confidential": kept on
# disk only, never redistributed (ref-docs/2026-11-15-sdram-datasheet-sources.md).
/ref-docs/Datasheets/*.pdf

# --- REFERENCE FIREWALL ---
# ref-proj/ held local clones of reference emulators used ONLY as black-box
# behavioural oracles. Mesen2, puNES, FCEUX and GeraNES are GPL; reproducing
# their source is what made RustyNES a derivative work (now GPL-3.0-or-later).
# The directory was REMOVED from disk and stays ignored as a guard so that
# source can never re-enter the working tree. Do NOT re-clone reference-emulator
# source into the repo; implement hardware behaviour from docs and test ROMs.
# (TriCNES, MIT, lives outside the repository at ~/reference-oracles/;
# guardrails section 3a.) See docs/ai-emulator-provenance-guardrails.md and the
# "MOST IMPORTANT RULE" of AGENTS.md.
/ref-proj/

# --- Temporary, merge and backup files ---
/tmp/
/temp/
*.tmp
# git conflict and `git apply --reject` leftovers.
*.orig
*.rej
# Pre-edit snapshots (`cp file file.bak`, `<file>.preedit`) an agent takes
# before instrumenting a file.
*.bak
*.preedit
# insta's pending inline-snapshot file.
*.pending-snap

# --- Environment / secrets ---
.env
.env.local

# --- Editors ---
.idea/
.vscode/
.zed/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# --- Android ---
# android/ has its own .gitignore; these cover the same outputs for a tool
# scanning from the root. The Gradle wrapper and keystore.properties.example
# are tracked.
android/**/build/
**/.gradle/
android/local.properties
android/app/src/main/jniLibs/
# Upload-signing secrets: the properties file at any depth, and any keystore.
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# --- iOS ---
# The xcframework, the UniFFI-generated Swift and the XcodeGen project are
# build artifacts (scripts/build-ios-xcframework.sh). The SwiftUI sources,
# project.yml, Info.plist, entitlements, PrivacyInfo, the bridging header and
# ios/Generated/.gitkeep are tracked.
ios/RustyNESFFI.xcframework/
ios/Generated/RustyNESCore.swift
ios/RustyNES.xcodeproj/
ios/build/
*.ipa
# fastlane output; the store listing under fastlane/metadata/ is tracked.
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/README.md
fastlane/test_output/

# --- Pre-commit ---
.pre-commit-cache/

# --- AI assistants and agent scratch ---
CLAUDE.local.md
/.claude/
.agents/
WARP.md
/.warp/
# The Antigravity PR reviewer's on-disk diff handoff (scripts/agy-review.sh),
# created and removed within one run.
/.agy-review-work/
# Review-round scratch an agent writes in the root: PR-thread dumps and one-shot
# patch scripts (thirteen sat untracked after #544). Root-anchored so nothing
# under scripts/ or crates/ matches.
/cr_*.json
/cr_*.txt
/fix_*.py
/*_comments.json
/threads.json
/unresolved_threads.txt
/pr_*.txt
# Local salvage of /tmp scratch, never part of the repo under either name
# (salvaged_tmp/ held session transcripts and the author's address, v3.2.0).
/salvaged/
/salvaged_tmp/

# --- Wiki (separate repository) ---
# A clone of github.com/doublegate/RustyNES.wiki.git, with its own .git.
/RustyNES.wiki/

# --- AccuracyCoin sub-test ROM builds ---
# The built ROMs under tests/roms/AccuracyCoin/sub-tests/ are tracked (with
# BUILD-PROVENANCE.tsv); an in-tree `--build-dir` and the nesasm listing and
# symbol sidecars are not.
/accuracycoin-build/
tests/roms/**/*.lst
tests/roms/**/*.fns
tests/roms/**/*.nl
